      text  of 
      cite@13:36
        item@13:37 hooley
          text Thm. 2
        item@13:54 landau
      text .
  section@15 1 1 intro
    heading
      text Introduction
    para@17 0
      text Landau 
      cite@17:8
        item@17:9 landau
      text  proved
    display@19
      line@19:5 asym B(x) ~ K x/sqrt(log x)
    para@21 0
      text By Theorem 
      ref@21:12 main
      text  and Lemmas 
      ref@21:29 a
      text  and 
      ref@21:36 b
      text , see (
      ref@21:45 asym
      text ) and Section 
      ref@21:64 intro
      text ; also 
      cite@22:6
        item@22:7 vallee
        item@22:16 erdos
        item@22:24 thesis
        item@22:33 arxiv
        item@22:41 parens
        item@22:50 dblp
        item@22:57 biblatex
      text  and 
      cite@22:72
        item@22:73 arxiv
          text §2
      text . The paper 
      cite@23:11
        item@23:11 hooley
      text  and the formula (
      ref@23:36 asym
      text ) are different things.
    theorem@25 theorem main
      heading
        text Main
      para@26 0
        text Every interval 
        math@26:19 [x, x + x^(1/4 + epsilon)]
        text  contains one.
    theorem@28 lemma a
      para@29 0
        text First.
    theorem@31 lemma b
      para@32 0
        text Second, by 
        cite@32:14
          item@32:15 landau
            text p. 
            math@32:28 305
        text .
  appendix@34
  section@36 1 1 comp
    heading
      text Computations
    theorem@38 lemma c
      para@39 0
        text As in Appendix 
        ref@39:18 comp
        text , Lemma 
        ref@39:31 c
        text  holds:
      display@41
        line@41:7 bound g(x) <= 2 x^(1/4)
